        "{\"event\":{\"at\":\"2026-11-03T20:45:43.284Z\",\"kind\":\"run.started\",\"payload\":{\"agent\":\"claude-code\"},\"signerFp\":\"411fcbf2fcfd3bf7ef10c75721a0c09fc8d7e44623e049fcf6be63d4ebd4e254\",\"subject\":\"01a1a329-1d21-7000-8efd-9a398ce3d8a2\",\"v\":1,\"which\":\"claude-code\",\"who\":\"mnid:e7e6f906a50be72b371e5f740adef221a62e3eb10bf7f5ebc955f1590b383519\"},\"link\":{\"hash\":\"931dfa1d152fae4bfdf0c565f7862d272e6e3333e2eaf4b97e6ab71533546c53\",\"prev\":\"807f3ea26260fcbc32a8338b621143d548a0db850868cdaf3b2da0e1d404dfe8\",\"seq\":1,\"tail\":\"411fcbf2fcfd3bf7ef10c75721a0c09fc8d7e44623e049fcf6be63d4ebd4e254-42fdc8309f2889b7f04a242837ab5758\"}}",
        "{\"event\":{\"at\":\"2026-11-03T20:45:43.331Z\",\"kind\":\"channel.served\",\"payload\":{},\"run\":\"01a1a329-1d21-7000-8efd-9a398ce3d8a2\",\"signerFp\":\"411fcbf2fcfd3bf7ef10c75721a0c09fc8d7e44623e049fcf6be63d4ebd4e254\",\"subject\":\"edit-rules-push\",\"v\":1,\"which\":\"claude-code\",\"who\":\"mnid:e7e6f906a50be72b371e5f740adef221a62e3eb10bf7f5ebc955f1590b383519\"},\"link\":{\"hash\":\"cbd0c92d35255eb0f310a6b7d6fc4c2da0487794b95ccf4366e8df3d07cfd8f3\",\"prev\":\"931dfa1d152fae4bfdf0c565f7862d272e6e3333e2eaf4b97e6ab71533546c53\",\"seq\":2,\"tail\":\"411fcbf2fcfd3bf7ef10c75721a0c09fc8d7e44623e049fcf6be63d4ebd4e254-42fdc8309f2889b7f04a242837ab5758\"}}",
        "{\"event\":{\"at\":\"2026-11-03T20:46:02.626Z\",\"kind\":\"decision.recorded\",\"payload\":{\"adr\":\"ADR-2\",\"alternatives\":\"Use `\\\\s+` after `export`: rejected, it behaves differently in JS (Unicode whitespace) and PHP (ASCII) and breaks parity. Strip `export` only after the comment and blank checks: rejected, `export # x=1` would then not behave as `# x=1` would, against \\\"exactly as if the prefix were not there\\\". Strip any `export` substring or an `export` without a following space: rejected, it would turn the legitimate keys `exportHOST` and `export` into something else. Change only the JS package: rejected by ADR-1, the gap is the defect.\",\"rationale\":\"`export KEY=value` must give the key `KEY`, exactly as if the prefix were absent. So the prefix (`^export[ \\\\t]+`, after trimming the line) is removed first, before the blank-line, `#`-comment and `=` checks, in `packages/js` and `packages/php` alike (ADR-1). Only a space or tab may follow `export`: JS `\\\\s` is Unicode-aware and PHP `\\\\s` is ASCII-only, so `[ \\\\t]` keeps the two packages identical. A bare `export`, `exportFOO=x`, `export=x`, `export NOEQUALS` and `export =x` are therefore not treated as prefixed assignments, and a `#` line stays a comment even when it mentions `export`. Both packages gained the same two tests.\",\"title\":\"EnvAccessor strips a leading `export` plus spaces or tabs before any other line check, in both packages\"},\"run\":\"01a1a329-1d21-7000-8efd-9a398ce3d8a2\",\"signerFp\":\"411fcbf2fcfd3bf7ef10c75721a0c09fc8d7e44623e049fcf6be63d4ebd4e254\",\"subject\":\"01a1a329-697c-7000-8fd1-58ae6863333b\",\"v\":1,\"which\":\"claude-code\",\"who\":\"mnid:e7e6f906a50be72b371e5f740adef221a62e3eb10bf7f5ebc955f1590b383519\"},\"link\":{\"hash\":\"e86e7fda1054a5f7469032b39df4be31541a2bc735bb7a5dc2f83c9a1c056418\",\"prev\":\"cbd0c92d35255eb0f310a6b7d6fc4c2da0487794b95ccf4366e8df3d07cfd8f3\",\"seq\":3,\"tail\":\"411fcbf2fcfd3bf7ef10c75721a0c09fc8d7e44623e049fcf6be63d4ebd4e254-42fdc8309f2889b7f04a242837ab5758\"}}",
